{"description":"Implement plugin command registration (B1): deferred registration from the plugin manifest into the cobra command tree, with the G-series trust boundary (official-registry-only, run-time hash verification, plugin dir over PATH, collision refusal, manifest cache) and registration failure semantics that never degrade the CLI.","acceptanceCriteria":"ADR-031 exists with contentState accepted documenting B1 deferred registration, the G1-G4 trust boundary, and the boundary vs ADR-022/023 (command surface != behavior layer). A plugin installed via the official registry registers its commands: each appears in eka --help with its group (dynamic grouping amendment applied to plan:cli-experience); execution dispatches to the plugin executable with bounded context; hash verified at dispatch (anti-TOCTOU); PATH-only plugins visibly refused; collisions with built-ins/other plugins refuse deterministically; probe timeout \u003c= 2s; broken plugin skipped with visible warning without breaking the CLI; manifest cached with TTL and invalidated on reinstall; per-process memoize."}